---
title: Product page
layout: home
description: One thing I own — what it replaced, what it cost, how it is actually used, and the honest paragraph about what is wrong with it.
eyebrow: Collections · Uses
source: src/components/ad.css · commerce.css
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap im-pt-sm im-section-sm">
	<p class="im-eyebrow">Collections · Uses · {{page.title}}</p>
	<p class="im-lede">{{page.description}}</p>
	<p class="doc-source"><code>{{page.source}}</code></p>
</section>

<div class="im-single im-wrap-wide im-single-aside-md" data-sidebar="on">
	<article class="im-stack im-stack-md">
		{{#with demo.uses.[0]}}
		<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb">
			<ol class="im-breadcrumb im-breadcrumb-chevron">
				<li><a href="/">{{> "icons/house"}}<span>Home</span></a></li>
				<li><a href="/collections/uses/">{{> "icons/package"}}<span>Uses</span></a></li>
				<li><span aria-current="page">{{name}}</span></li>
			</ol>
		</nav>

		<header class="im-stack im-stack-xs">
			<p class="im-snipcard-meta"><span class="im-kind" data-kind="issue">{{> "icons/package"}}Owned</span><span>{{by}}</span><span>Bought {{bought}}</span></p>
			<h1 class="im-collhead-title">{{name}}</h1>
			<p class="im-rating im-rating-lg" style="--im-rating: 4.5"><span class="im-rating-stars" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="im-rating-value">4.5 out of 5</span><span>after 7 months</span></p>
		</header>

		<figure class="im-projectcover" style="--im-projectcover-ratio: 16 / 10"><img src="{{../demo.shots.[0]}}" alt="" loading="eager"></figure>

		<div class="im-expstats">
			<span><strong>{{cost}}</strong>Paid</span>
			<span><strong>7 mo</strong>Owned</span>
			<span><strong>~2,400</strong>Frames</span>
			<span><strong>Daily</strong>Used</span>
		</div>
		{{/with}}

		<section class="im-content im-content-flush im-content-lede">
			<p>It replaced a body I had carried for three years and had stopped taking anywhere, because it was heavy enough that leaving it behind was always the easier decision. That is the whole review: the best camera argument is not about sensors.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="im-content im-content-flush">
			<h2>How I actually use it</h2>
			<p>One lens, no bag, in a coat pocket. It lives on <strong>aperture priority at f/4</strong> with auto ISO capped at 6400 and exposure compensation on the front dial, and I have not changed those settings since the first week.</p>
			<p>Every photograph on this site since March is from it, including the ones that look like they were taken on something bigger. The <a href="/collections/travel/trip/">Amalfi trip</a> was six days, four hundred frames and one battery charge a day.</p>

			<h2>What is wrong with it</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>The battery.</strong> Three hundred frames on paper, about two hundred in the cold. Buy two spares before you buy anything else.</li>
				<li><strong>The close focus is soft wide open.</strong> Everybody writes this and everybody is right.</li>
				<li><strong>It is not weather sealed</strong> without the filter and adapter, which is a fifty-euro asterisk on the price.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>What I would buy instead</h2>
			<p>Nothing at this price. At half of it, a used body from two generations ago and the same lens — you lose the viewfinder and you keep the pictures.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="im-section im-section-tight">
			<h2 class="im-caption" data-index="with">Used with</h2>
			<div class="im-affiliates">
				{{#each demo.uses}}{{#match group "=" "Camera"}}{{#match @index ">" 0}}
				<article class="im-affiliate">
					<span class="im-affiliate-media im-thumb"><img src="{{lookup ../../demo.shots @index}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></span>
					<a class="im-affiliate-name" href="/collections/uses/page/">{{name}}</a>
					<p class="im-affiliate-by">{{by}}</p>
					<p class="im-affiliate-text">{{text}}</p>
					<p class="im-affiliate-meta"><span class="im-affiliate-price">{{cost}}</span><span class="im-badge im-badge-success">Still using it</span></p>
				</article>
				{{/match}}{{/match}}{{/each}}
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="im-section im-section-tight">
			<h2 class="im-caption" data-index="pictures">In use</h2>
			<div class="im-bento">
				{{#each demo.shots}}<a class="im-bento-cell im-zoomable" href="{{this}}" data-caption="In use"><img src="{{this}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></a>{{/each}}
			</div>
		</section>

		{{> "components/comments" thread=demo.comments count="18"}}
	</article>

	<aside>
		<div class="im-sticky-rail">
			<div class="im-widgets">
				{{#with demo.author}}{{> "components/author-widget"}}{{/with}}
				<section class="im-widget im-widget-accent" aria-labelledby="up-buy">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="up-buy">Where I got it</h2>
					<p class="im-widget-heading">€1,599, from a shop with a real returns desk.</p>
					<a class="im-btn im-btn-primary im-btn-sm im-w-full" href="#" rel="sponsored noopener">{{icon "external-link"}}The shop</a>
					<p class="im-affiliate-mark im-mt-sm" title="Affiliate link — I earn a little if you buy, at no cost to you">{{icon "info"}}Affiliate link. It is on this page because I bought it.</p>
				</section>

				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="up-facts">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="up-facts">The facts</h2>
					<dl class="im-widget-facts">
						<dt>Bought</dt><dd>March 2026</dd>
						<dt>Paid</dt><dd>€1,599</dd>
						<dt>Replaced</dt><dd>A heavier body</dd>
						<dt>Verdict</dt><dd>Keeping</dd>
						<dt>Group</dt><dd><a href="/collections/uses/">For making video</a></dd>
					</dl>
				</section>

				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="up-recent">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="up-recent">Recently bought <a href="/collections/uses/">All</a></h2>
					<div class="im-widget-products">
						{{#each demo.uses}}{{#match @index ">" 4}}<a class="im-widget-product" href="/collections/uses/page/"><img src="{{lookup ../demo.shots @index}}" alt="" loading="lazy"><span class="im-widget-product-name">{{name}}</span><span class="im-widget-product-note">{{cost}}</span>{{icon "arrow-right"}}</a>{{/match}}{{/each}}
					</div>
				</section>

				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="up-seen">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="up-seen">Seen in</h2>
					<ul class="im-widget-list">
						<li><a href="/collections/travel/trip/">The Amalfi Coast, slowly<small>Every frame</small></a></li>
						<li><a href="/collections/video/page/">Driving the Amalfi Coast<small>The whole video</small></a></li>
						<li><a href="/collections/experience/page/">Diving the Blue Hole<small>In a housing</small></a></li>
					</ul>
				</section>

				<section class="im-widget im-widget-fill" aria-labelledby="up-sub">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="up-sub">When this page changes</h2>
					<p class="im-widget-heading">Twice a year, at most.</p>
					{{> "components/subscribe" id="use-email" button="Tell me"}}
				</section>
			</div>
		</div>
	</aside>
</div>

<section class="im-section im-wrap">
	<div class="im-prose">
		<h2>A uses page is a review collection, not a shopping list</h2>
		<p>A list of product names with affiliate links is an advertisement with a personal pronoun in it. What makes the page worth reading is the three headings this one has, and none of them can be written by somebody who does not own the thing:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>How I actually use it</strong> — the settings, the routine, the thing it goes in.</li>
			<li><strong>What is wrong with it</strong> — the page has no credibility without this, and the credibility is the only reason anybody clicks the link.</li>
			<li><strong>What I would buy instead</strong> — including "nothing", which is a real answer.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>The disclosure is a mark, not a paragraph</h2>
		<p><code>im-affiliate-mark</code> sits in the meta row, before the link, with the long form in its <code>title</code>. It used to be a line of its own on every card, which cost the card a row and made a page of eight things as tall as a page of eight posts. Saying it once per card, small, next to the price, is both honest and the right size.</p>
		<div class="im-table-scroll">
		<table>
			<thead><tr><th>Class</th><th></th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>im-usegroup</code></td><td>A group with its own heading — "on the desk", "for making video". Forty unsorted objects is an inventory; four groups of ten is a page.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-affiliate</code></td><td>The line item: picture, name, maker, two clamped lines, price, verdict, disclosure.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-rating</code></td><td>The score after living with it, with <em>how long</em> beside it. A rating written on the day it arrived is worth nothing.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>im-widget-products</code></td><td>"Recently bought" in the rail — the one widget this collection needs that no other one does.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
